# FS02-060: registry-v0 is PR-based and operator-merged. There is no self-service write
# path at v0 — every change to the registry is reviewed and merged by the steward operator.
#
# Dated note, 2026-09-08: every owner below is the organisation OWNER's login, not a
# team. It used to name a `stewards` team of this organisation, and no such team exists
# — a CODEOWNERS file naming a team that does not exist silently reviews nothing, which
# is worse than no file: GitHub cannot request a review from an owner it cannot resolve,
# so a "required review from Code Owners" rule can be satisfied by nobody at all. A
# login GitHub can resolve is strictly better than a team it cannot.
#
# Two things this does NOT do. It does not make review required: branch protection
# carries no required-review rule while the organisation has a single admin, who cannot
# review their own pull request in any case. And it does not settle the owner for good:
# creating the team, putting its members in it and turning the required-review rule on
# is one operator act, tracked as PS-O14, and this file names the team again on the day
# the team exists. Verify on the first pull request that a review is actually requested.
#
# Superseded wording: "[HUMAN TODO] Replace the placeholder team with the real one once
# the GitHub org exists and branch protection is configured."

*                       @DimitrieVatra

